LAMMPS (22 Jul 2025 - Update 3)
# Example 6.4 (strongly attractive wall, eps_w = 3, T* = 0.90) -- Lennard-Jones fluid in a slit pore (reduced units)
# Liquid slab (interface normal along x) between two structureless 9-3 walls at z = 0 and z = H.
# Same potential, cutoff, thermostat, time step, cross-section and run schedule as Example 6.2.
# usage:  lmp -in in.pore                      (run inside the folder strong/T0.90/; the settings are below)
units           lj
atom_style      atomic
boundary        p p f                # periodic along x and y, walls (non-periodic) along z

variable        T       index 0.90
variable        epsw    index 3.0         # wall strength epsilon_w / epsilon_ff
variable        rcw     index 4.0       # wall cutoff; 0.8579 = (2/5)^(1/6) cuts the 9-3 potential at its minimum (purely repulsive wall)
variable        H       index 7.0         # wall separation Setting up Verlet run ...
